The behavior described occurs because BGP sessions rely on the TCP connection and hold timer, not direct route availability. To ensure immediate termination upon route loss, bind BGP sessions to the specific interface used to reach the peer. If the interface's route disappears, the session terminates instantly. Use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
