To gracefully suspend BGP session monitoring during maintenance without affecting the control plane stability, use the `shutdown` command under the relevant BGP monitor hierarchy. This administratively disables monitoring while preserving all configurations.

**Deactivate BGP monitoring per neighbor:**
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip> monitor shutdown
```

**Deactivate BGP monitoring per group:**
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> monitor shutdown
```

**Deactivate global BGP monitoring:**
```cli
configure router bgp monitor shutdown
```

After maintenance, re-enable monitoring using `no shutdown` in the same context. For example:
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip> monitor no shutdown
