2. **`keepalive 60`**  
   - Configures BGP keepalive messages to be sent every 60 seconds (one-third of the hold time, per BGP standards).

### Implementation Notes:
- Replace `<group_name>` and `<ip_address>` with your specific BGP group or neighbor IP.
- Apply these commands selectively to peers traversing high-latency links to avoid unnecessary timer increases for other sessions.
- The `min` parameter prevents sessions from establishing if the peer proposes a hold time below 180 seconds, ensuring compatibility.
